  "intro": [
    "Copper bonded earth rods conform to BS 4360 grade 43A. They are made from drawn high tensile, low carbon steel with a deposition of 99.9% pure electrolytic copper. Electrolytic deposition gives a molecular bond between the two metals; the copper layer is generally up to 250 microns. Threads are formed by roll threading, which keeps strength and maintains the bonded copper along the full length of the threads.",
    "Solid copper earth rods are drawn from high conductivity copper and suit extreme soil conditions, where salt or moisture content is high. They are highly resistant to corrosion, which gives a longer life. External threads are roll formed; internally threaded rods are also available.",
    "Hot dip galvanized steel earth rods, made of high strength low carbon steel and galvanized to BS 729, are a cost effective option for earthing."
  ],
